1254
00:57:39.900 --> 00:57:52.680
And so what I found was, oh, my gosh, the material and characters that I saw at that wedding and that life experience I got from going to that thing is just going to feed my art.

1255
00:57:52.680 --> 00:57:56.820
So it's like you can't do art if you're just doing art.

1256
00:57:56.980 --> 00:57:57.140
Right.

1257
00:57:57.200 --> 00:57:59.980
I think you have to have a whole life in order to feed it.

1258
00:58:00.400 --> 00:58:06.180
And an identity that's like where you're like self-esteem is a little bit more like diversified.

1259
00:58:06.180 --> 00:58:12.740
In other words, if your whole worth originates from your ability to do this one thing and you're not doing that one thing, then you're kind of a ghoSt.

1260
00:58:13.580 --> 00:58:16.540
So like to have like if you're like, oh, yeah, I'm not just an actor.

1261
00:58:16.720 --> 00:58:20.120
I'm someone's mom or I'm someone's right, you know, or I'm or not someone's.

1262
00:58:20.180 --> 00:58:21.220
I am a mom.

1263
00:58:21.360 --> 00:58:23.740
I am a bicycle enthusiaSt.

1264
00:58:23.840 --> 00:58:25.040
I am a whatever a volunteer.

1265
00:58:25.300 --> 00:58:30.520
I you know, then you then it's not like, oh, when I'm auditioning for a part, I'm auditioning for my self-worth.

1266
00:58:30.800 --> 00:58:32.400
It's like I'm just auditioning for the part.

1267
00:58:32.660 --> 00:58:35.840
It's like, yeah, which is hard enough or daunting enough.

1268
00:58:35.980 --> 00:58:36.580
That makes sense.

1269
00:58:36.680 --> 00:58:37.140
That's beautiful.

